{"url": "https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/academic/language.do", "final_url": "https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/academic/language.do", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-15", "text": "\ub300\ud559\uc6d0(\uc601\ubb38) | Academic Guide | Language/International | TOEFL\n\ubcf8\ubb38 \ubc14\ub85c\uac00\uae30\n\uc8fc\uba54\ub274 \ubc14\ub85c\uac00\uae30\n\uc11c\ube0c\uba54\ub274 \ubc14\ub85c\uac00\uae30\nyoutube\ninsta\nHOME\nSITEMAP\nLANGUAGE\nKOREAN\nAbout Yonsei\nDean's Welcome\nAbout Graduate School\nGraduate School Introduction\nMap to Yonsei\nAdmission\nSubmission Schedule\nInt'l Student Track\nGKS Program\nOn-Campus Housing\nSuccessful Announcement\nAcademic Guide\nAcademic Calendar\nRegistration\nSign up\nAcademic\nThesis/Graduation\nScholarship\nLanguage/International\nNews\nNews\nYonsei Chunchu\nYonsei Annals\nK-STAR Visa Track\nBK21\nVision&Goal\nInnovation Program\nGlobal Advisory Committee\nInnovation Program Guide\nNotice\nNotice\n\ubaa8\ubc14\uc77c \uba54\ub274 \uc5f4\uae30\nAbout Yonsei\nDean's Welcome\nAbout Graduate School\nGraduate School Introduction\nOrganization\nDepartments List\nMap to Yonsei\nAdmission\nSubmission Schedule\nInt'l Student Track\nSpring\nFall\nGKS Program\nOn-Campus Housing\nSuccessful Announcement\nAcademic Guide\nAcademic Calendar\nRegistration\nRegular registration\nRegistration for extra semesters\nTuition refund\nSign up\nGrades\nEnrolment\nSubject\nAcademic\nLeave of absence\nReturn to school\nReadmission\nVoluntary withdrawal\nCourse change\netc\nThesis/Graduation\nDegree conferment requirements\nDissertation process\nGuide to thesis qualification and qualification test\nHow to write a dissertation\nHow to submit a thesis qualification\nApplicants who are expected to end the semester\nScholarship\nOn-campus scholarship\nForeigner Special Scholarship\nOff-campus scholarship\nScholarship application and payment\nLanguage/International\nTOEFL\nDual Degree\nReview of Dual Degree\nForeigner\nNews\nNews\nYonsei Chunchu\nYonsei Annals\nK-STAR Visa Track\nBK21\nVision&Goal\nInnovation Program\nGlobal Advisory Committee\nInnovation Program Guide\nNotice\nNotice\n\ubaa8\ubc14\uc77c \uba54\ub274 \ub2eb\uae30\nAcademic Guide\nHome\nAcademic Guide\nAbout Yonsei\nAdmission\nAcademic Guide\nNews\nBK21\nNotice\nLanguage/International\nAcademic Calendar\nRegistration\nSign up\nAcademic\nThesis/Graduation\nScholarship\nLanguage/International\nTOEFL\nTOEFL\nDual Degree\nReview of Dual Degree\nForeigner\nAcademic Calendar\nRegistration\nRegular registration\nRegistration for extra semesters\nTuition refund\nSign up\nGrades\nEnrolment\nSubject\nAcademic\nLeave of absence\nReturn to school\nReadmission\nVoluntary withdrawal\nCourse change\netc\nThesis/Graduation\nDegree conferment requirements\nDissertation process\nGuide to thesis qualification and qualification test\nHow to write a dissertation\nHow to submit a thesis qualification\nApplicants who are expected to end the semester\nScholarship\nOn-campus scholarship\nForeigner Special Scholarship\nOff-campus scholarship\nScholarship application and payment\nLanguage/International\nTOEFL\nDual Degree\nReview of Dual Degree\nForeigner\nThe graduate school holds an Yonsei TOEFL every semester for language requirements as a part of graduate school admission and/or thesis submission qualification.\nAny alterations on the TOEFL test schedule will be announced separately (schedules may be canceled)\nCancellation of test registration: Cancellations are accepted for those made during the registration period (after the registration period, cancellation is not accepted).\n1. Schedule\n\ubcf5\ud559 \uc2e0\uccad\uc808\ucc28 \ud45c\n\ud69f\uc218\n\ud559\uae30\n\uc811\uc218\uae30\uac04\n\uc2dc\ud5d8\uc2dc\ud589\uc77c\n\uc8fc\uad00\ubd80\uc11c\n\uc678\uad6d\uc5b4\uc2dc\ud5d8(\uc790\uaca9\uc2dc\ud5d8)\ud569\uaca9 \uc778\uc815 \uc81c\ucd9c \uae30\ud55c\n1\n1\ud559\uae30\n3\uc6d4\n4\uc6d4\n\ub300\ud559\uc6d0\n2\n2\ud559\uae30\n9\uc6d4\n10\uc6d4\n\ucd94\ud6c4 \uc548\ub0b4 \uc608\uc815\n2. Method\nA. Uses the PBT method written from ETS\nB. Test Formation\nSection \u2160: 35 minutes Listening Comprehension\nSection \u2161: 25 minutes Structure\nSection \u2162: 55 minutes Reading\nC. What to prepare\n1) Formal identification card [identification card, driver\u2019s license, passport (must be a valid passport before the expiry date)- choose one]\n2) Writing supplies (pencil or a mechanical pencil, eraser)\n3. Process\nA. From the bottom of the Yonsei University graduate school webpage, click on Yonsei TOEFL from the Yonsei Quick menu, and register from the TOEFL registration webpage (https://b2b.toiec.co.kr/yonsei)\nB. Test Location: YBM Language Institute Shinchon B1 CBT test site [113 Sinchon-ro, Sinchon-dong, Seodaemun-gu, Seoul]\nC. Announcement of results: check https://ipresult.toeflitp.co.kr after 3PM on results day\nYou may issue or print out the test results (*You may issue up to three sheets of test results and if you wish to issue extra, submit an explanatory statement on the result page and you may issue up to three result sheets)\n4. Notices\nA. Only students who have passed the qualifying exams (language and comprehensive exams) in the previous semester are eligible to submit a 'Thesis Research Proposal.'\nB. The results of the qualifying exams (foreign language exams) must be reported to the graduate school through the department within the designated period during the 1st or 2nd semester. Students who fail the qualifying exams are not allowed to submit their thesis research proposal in the following semester.\nC. Failure to submit or delay in submitting the qualifying exam results may cause delays in the thesis review schedule and graduation process, so it is essential to submit them within the deadline.\nAddress : 03722 Yonsei University Graduate School, 50 Yonsei-Ro, Seodaemun-Gu, Seoul, South Korea, ,\nMail : Ysgrad@yonsei.ac.kr\ncopyrights (C) 2017 Yonsei Graduate School. All rights r